// Reading the ZIP CONTAINER a .pdb is, as a host service.
//
// The pdb FORMAT stays in Pure — what a table holds, how elements and sections
// are laid out, what has to match a golden. The container does not: every host
// already ships a zip reader (java.util.zip, node/browser zip.js), and doing it
// in Pure instead meant each platform ran a translated bit-at-a-time DEFLATE.
// On the Java platform that was most of a suite run.
//
// An entry is addressed by NAME. Nothing here exposes offsets, compression
// methods or sizes: a caller only ever wants what is in the archive and the
// bytes of one entry.

native function meta::pure::compiler::pdb::archive::entryNames(archive:Binary[1]):String[*];

native function meta::pure::compiler::pdb::archive::entryBytes(archive:Binary[1], name:String[1]):Binary[1];
